 in code by comparing unique and overall occurrences of operators and operands, associated with maintainability.\ndf['redundancy_indicator'] = 1 - ((df['uniq_Op'] + df['uniq_Opnd']) / (df['n'] + 1e-10))", "# v_g_scaled_by_difficulty\n# Cyclomatic complexity scaled by Halstead difficulty (v(g) * d).\n# Usefulness: Combines two important indicators of code complexity to emphasize how structural and logical complexity interact.\ndf['v_g_scaled_by_difficulty'] = df['v(g)'] * df['d']", "# density_complexity\n# Complexity density reflecting how cyclomatic complexity scales with combined code size (v(g) / (loc + lOCode)).\n# Usefulness: Integrates structural complexity relative to total code and comment lines, capturing control flow density.\ndf['density_complexity'] = df['v(g)'] / ((df['loc'] + df['lOCode']) + 1e-10)", "# code_effort_alignment\n# Code effort alignment score (e / loc_code_and_comment).\n# Usefulness: Indicates the alignment of effort required for a module relative to its overall size (code and comments).\ndf['code_effort_alignment'] = df['e'] / ((df['loc'] + df['lOCode'] + df['lOComment']) + 1e-10)", "# effective_volume_per_line\n# Effective Halstead volume per line of code (v / loc).\n# Usefulness: Highlights the computational work embedded per line of code, indirectly indicating complexity intensity.\ndf['effective_volume_per_line'] = df['v'] / (df['loc'] + 1e-10)", "# threshold_complexity_flag\n# Binary flag indicating high cyclomatic complexity (v(g) > 10).\n# Usefulness: Identifies thresholds for high-complexity modules, aiding in detecting extreme cases related to defects.\ndf['threshold_complexity_flag'] = (df['v(g)'] > 10).astype(int)", "df.drop(columns=['complexity_per_uniq_operator', 'loc_effort_ratio'], inplace=True)"]
